 ### Data Models (`Models.swift`)
 
 - **`TaskMode`** — `.carryOver` (rolls if incomplete), `.repeating` (every week), `.oneTime` (never carries)
-- **`TaskType`** — `.checkbox`, `.goal` (target/progress/unit) or `.list` (items stored as sub-tasks; checks itself off). Type and mode are independent.
+- **`TaskType`** — `.checkbox`, `.goal` (target/progress/unit) or `.list` (items stored as sub-tasks; checks itself off; `isListFolded` saves its fold, `isFolded` is that for lists only). Type and mode are independent.
 - **`SubTask`**, **`ChecklistTask`**, **`Category`** (name + SF Symbol + tasks)
 - **`Week`** — container of categories, identified by `startDay` (a `DayKey`: Gregorian year-month-day, saved as `"yyyy-MM-dd"`), not by a moment, so time-zone changes can't duplicate weeks. `startDate` is computed (midnight in the current time zone) and still written for older builds; files without `startDay` get it from `startDate` in the current time zone on first load and are re-saved. `dismissedCarryOvers` / `dismissedRepeating` record tasks the user deleted from that week.
 - **`GoalNumber`** — locale-aware goal amount parsing/formatting; goal values are capped at `GoalUnitKind.maxValue` (999,999)
@@ -113,6 +113,7 @@ Key behaviors:
 - **Add Category**: a "This week only" toggle (off = every week) applies to whatever is added next; no second dialog. A category added for this week only is kept in Saved Categories too (ones from before are saved at launch, `saveThisWeekOnlyCategories`, unless removed there).
 - **This week only on a card**: a card's own edit mode has a This week only switch (`ThisWeekOnlyToggle`, `store.setCategoryThisWeekOnly`) where the Add task row is outside edit mode (the row stays mounted, showing nothing, with `isEditing`: a Smart Add still working adds its task when done, and words typed but not added are added as editing starts; removed, it lost both), so no row moves as editing starts (with it under the card's name, the rows slid down and a tap meant for a delete button opened a sub-task field). On: its carry-over and repeating tasks become one-time, each remembering its mode (`ChecklistTask.modeBeforeThisWeekOnly`: the mode and whether the user had changed the task, saved in checklist.json), and later weeks lose the category, keeping only tasks the user added or changed there. Off: the tasks get their modes back exactly as before (`restoreModes`), and it comes back next week. Adding a carry-over or repeating task to such a card, or changing a task to one, turns it off (`keepCategory`) and puts the other tasks' modes back the same way; the picker's hint says so. A mode the user picks for a task replaces its remembered one. Carry-over and repeating copies that sync brings into a later week's This week only card arrive one-time too, remembering their mode (`arriving`); sync still follows, removes and keeps them deleted by that mode (`syncMode`), so they leave with a finished source and a deleted one stays deleted.
 - **Reordering tasks**: in a card's edit mode each task has a drag handle. Touching it lifts the task at once (a medium haptic, 3% larger, on its own outlined card with a shadow, `LiftedTaskBackground`); it follows the finger and the tasks it passes slide over to make room (a selection tick for each), and letting go drops it there (`TaskReorder` in CategoryCard.swift: frames measured outside the offsets in the `taskList` coordinate space and snapshotted at the lift; it takes a task's place on reaching its middle, going up or down, and can't be dragged past either end). The handle's `DragGesture(minimumDistance: 0)` reads the finger in `.global` (its own space moves with the lifted row, the list's with the grid as it scrolls); the task's distance in the list is that move plus how far the grid has scrolled since the lift. Held within 72pt of the top (below the header, the scroll view's top inset) or bottom (above the bottom bar, `cardGridBottomBar` in the environment), the grid scrolls, up to 900pt/s at the edge (`TaskAutoScroller`, TaskAutoScroller.swift: it finds the page's `UIScrollView` from a plain view inside the card, `TaskAutoScrollAnchor`, and moves its content offset each frame with a display link, outside SwiftUI state), once the finger has moved 8pt and until the task reaches that end of its card. The lifted row's `zIndex` is its last modifier: before `onGeometryChange` the stack ignored it, and rows it passed while scrolling were drawn over it. No system drag and drop (`.draggable`): its task lifted only after a hold, showed only a small copy under the finger, and a sideways wobble meanwhile swiped the week. While a task is lifted `store.isReorderingTask` keeps the week swipe from starting (`@ObservationIgnored`, read only by the gesture). VoiceOver gets Move Up / Move Down. `store.moveTask` records the category in the week's `userOrderedCategories`, so syncing with the week before leaves that order alone.
+- **Folding lists**: a list has a chevron just before its type/mode button (`foldButton`; down while open, turned to the side while folded, mirrored right to left; VoiceOver "Collapse list" / "Expand list" with the list's name as its value). Folded, the items and the Add Item row are hidden and the row shows how many items are checked ("2 of 5", `foldedCount`; nothing for an empty list). A new list, or a task that becomes one, is open (`updateTaskType` clears the fold). Folding adds what was typed in Add Item first, and an item being renamed saves as its row goes (`SubTaskRowCard`'s `onDisappear`). `store.setListFolded` isn't an edit: no `isUserEdited`, no card edit time, and a delete's Undo stays (`save(keepsUndo: true)`). Carried and repeating copies take the fold when they're made (`carriedCopy`, `resetRecurringTask`), and folding also sets it on the list's untouched copies in later saved weeks (`foldLaterCopies`, along `carriedFrom`/`repeatsFrom`), so it's still folded next week; sync's follow never changes a fold, so one changed in a later week stays. Past weeks show every list open (view only). The chevron stays in a card's edit mode.
 - **Header**: `Week.displayTitle` is "Week of Oct 5" in the user's locale, with the year only when it isn't this year.
 - **Haptics**: light tap on ticking a task, selection on sub-tasks, success on finishing a goal or a whole card (keyed by category ID so paging weeks is silent). Closed cards with no tasks say "No tasks yet · Tap to add"; a ring is grey until something is done; done tasks are struck through.
 - **Tasks**: checking a task with sub-tasks (or a list) checks them all; unchecking puts back the checks from before (cleared if there were none). Edits that change nothing (same name, same mode) don't mark a task `isUserEdited`. Typed but unadded tasks and sub-tasks are added however the keyboard closes; closing a card dismisses the keyboard first. Cards lift for dragging after a 0.5s hold. Tapping a task's or sub-task's name renames it. An open card also closes from a tap on its icon or name.
